course: dictionary
lesson: 7617
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Privy is one of them. In an old story, «The privy» at the bottom of the garden is an outdoor toilet: a small hut over a hole in the ground.
explain: Look at the words around privy to find its meaning. «I wasn't privy to their plans» has the words plans and their. Someone was keeping secret plans, and the speaker was not allowed to know them. So privy to means allowed to know a secret.
explain: Privy can also be part of a title. The Privy Council is a group that advises the king or queen. The capital letters and the word Council are the clues here: it is a name for a group, not a hut. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it fits.
fact: Privy can be a noun or an adjective.
fact: As a noun, «privy» means an old outdoor toilet.
fact: «Privy to» means allowed to know a secret, as in «I wasn't privy to their plans».
fact: The Privy Council is a UK group that advises the king or queen.
fact: Privy is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in history books, old stories and the news.
exercise: «The privy» stood at the bottom of the garden in the old story. What is a privy? | A tall tree with thick leaves | A secret plan | A kind of bread | *A small outdoor toilet
exercise: «I wasn't privy to their plans.» What does privy to mean here? | *Allowed to know a secret | Angry about the plans | Ready to leave early | Painting the plans on a wall
exercise: What is the Privy Council? | A type of garden shed | A team of footballers | *A group that advises the king or queen | A school club for reading
test: In the title Privy Council, which clue tells you it is a group and not a hut? | *The capital letters and the word Council | The word garden | The word privy on its own | The word old
test: «She was privy to the news before anyone else.» What does privy to mean? | *Knew a secret before others | Lived in a small hut | Forgot the news | Was cold and wet
exam: In «He was privy to the secret plan», what does privy to mean? | Was lost in the garden | Was tired of waiting | Was angry about the plan | *Was allowed to know the secret
